1. AI SOLUTION
Plant diseases pose a threat to global food security and agricultural productivity.
Diagnosing Plant diseases takes a lot of time and needs many resources and expertise. 
Farmers and other agricultural practitioners usually check leaves by hand. 
This manual inspection of symptoms is easy to make mistakes,
especially in places that do not have many resources. Smallholder farmers and
agricultural extension officers find it hard to identify Plant diseases quickly because they do not have access to plant pathologists or diagnostic services.
We plan to use the PlantVillage dataset. This dataset contains thousands of plant leaf images that have already been checked by experts.
The dataset is quality and reliable.
We will build a tool that helps practitioners and farmers detect and classify foliar diseases. The tool uses learning for image classification. 
It can recognise 38 Plant diseases across 14 key crop species: Apple, Blueberry, Cherry, Corn,
Grape, Orange, Peach, Bell Pepper, Potato, Raspberry, Soybean, Squash, Strawberry and Tomato.
This AI solution matches South African goals of using AI technologies to build new tools for agriculture.
The solution will lower the workload. 
It will give a path from detection to corrective actions, for Plant diseases that threaten crops.
It will also bring expertise to smallholder farmers who cannot afford or reach expert plant pathologists.

Primary Objectives:
 Increase the accuracy of plant disease diagnosis to than 75% using the PlantVillage dataset
 Cut down the time needed for disease diagnosis from days to just seconds
 Boost crop prognosis by detecting diseases early and helping farmers make smart agricultural decisions
 Lower agricultural losses and reduce input costs for farmers while still maintaining high crop quality
 Expand access to plant disease diagnosis in low-resource and rural areas
 Show how AgriScan AI can automate the process of diagnosing plant diseases in agriculture.

Scalability & Growth:
 Build methods that can be applied to a wider range of agricultural imaging tasks such as stem, root and fruit diseases
 Design a system that allows for continuous updates and expansion of the dataset, with regional disease data
 Create a full ecosystem of tools and services that grow from the foundation of the PlantVillage dataset
 Allow the system to connect with IoT sensors for complete plant health monitoring
 Support the detection of multiple diseases at once especially in cases of complex plant infections.




